  "benchmark": "A frozen learned policy plays at least 100,000 fresh 200bb HUNL Slumbot hands, scores above 0 bb/100, and has a 95% confidence-interval lower bound above 0.",
  "hypothesis": "The prior zero-signal ES smoke is explained by unit-direction perturbations that were too small to cross Standard10 greedy margins; an outcome-blind geometric sigma scan will identify a cap-safe dose with median 1-8% and target approximately 3% action disagreement across every mirrored direction.",
  "material_change": "Query 4,096 fresh balanced reachable states under the exact Standard10-plus-random-feature residual initialization and the exact eight ES directions. Scan sigma 0.005 through 0.8, measure action disagreement and residual-logit magnitude only, use no rewards or environment outcomes, and select a dose by preregistered activation bounds.",
  "baseline": "At sigma 0.005, two fresh 6,144-hand generations produced exactly zero fitness differences and zero learned-weight update. This calibration determines whether the cause is perturbation scale rather than ES strength.",
