  "result": {
    "summary": "An outcome-blind scan queried the exact eight mirrored ES directions over 4,096 fresh balanced states at eight geometric sigmas. Median greedy disagreement rose from 0 at sigma 0.005 to 1.2695% at sigma 0.8; the selected dose spanned 0.8301%-1.8799% across directions and kept the maximum residual logit near 0.2001 under the 0.25 cap. All 264 tests passed.",
    "conclusion": "The prior two-generation zero-fitness result was caused by an inactive perturbation dose, not evidence against direct-greedy ES. Sigma 0.8 is the smallest scanned dose satisfying the preregistered 1-8% median activation band with every direction nonzero and cap-safe behavior. This is an outcome-blind activation result only and makes no strength claim.",
    "decision": "ADMIT_SIGMA0P8_GREEDY_ES_MINIMAL_SIGNAL_RETRY",
    "next_step": "Run one minimal fresh mirrored generation at sigma 0.8 with the same six opponents and both seats. Require nonzero fitness differences, positive split-half direction correlation, a nonzero trust-region-bounded center update, and untouched holdout direction agreement before considering a second generation or multi-seed geometric scale."
  },
